  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.3</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> is along the positive <math> <mtext>Z</mtext> </math> -direction. A rectangular loop (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></math>) of sides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math> carries a current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. Out of the following different orientations which one corresponds to stable equilibrium?",
